0.100 0.220 0.420 RG 1.20 w 45.00 365.00 m 567.00 365.00 l S
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 11 Tf 45.00 347.00 Td (3.1 Safe /proc/[pid]/stat Parsing \(Member 1\)) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 333.00 Td (Linux process names in /proc/[pid]/stat are enclosed in parentheses and may contain spaces or embedded) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 320.50 Td (parentheses \(e.g. '\(Web Content\)'\). Standard scanf or strtok approaches fail catastrophically. The) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 308.00 Td (Guardian solves this by locating the first '\(' with strchr\(\) and the last '\)' with strrchr\(\), safely) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 295.50 Td (copying the command name and parsing subsequent state, ppid, user ticks, and kernel ticks from the) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 283.00 Td (remainder of the line.) Tj ET
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 11 Tf 45.00 260.50 Td (3.2 CPU Utilization Calculation \(Member 1\)) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 246.50 Td (CPU utilization is calculated across consecutive sampling snapshots using the exact formula:) Tj ET
0.950 0.960 0.970 rg 0.780 0.820 0.860 RG 45.00 183.00 522.00 47.00 re B
0.100 0.150 0.250 rg BT /F3 8.0 Tf 55.00 218.00 Td (ticks_per_sec = sysconf\(_SC_CLK_TCK\);) Tj ET
0.100 0.150 0.250 rg BT /F3 8.0 Tf 55.00 207.00 Td (delta_ticks   = current.total_cpu_ticks - previous.total_cpu_ticks;) Tj ET
0.100 0.150 0.250 rg BT /F3 8.0 Tf 55.00 196.00 Td (cpu_usage_pct = \(\(delta_ticks / \(double\)ticks_per_sec\) / elapsed_seconds\) * 100.0;) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 175.00 Td (The calculated value reflects the percentage of one logical CPU core \(0.0% to 100.0%+\), matching standard) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 162.50 Td (top behavior without requiring system-wide tick normalization or multi-core division.) Tj ET
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 11 Tf 45.00 140.00 Td (3.3 Anomaly Detection & Active Suppression \(Member 3\)) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.5 Tf 45.00 126.00 Td (To avoid alert fatigue, the anomaly detector enforces a strict persistence and suppression contract:) Tj ET
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 10.0 Tf 48.00 109.50 Td (•) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.0 Tf 59.00 109.50 Td (Threshold Criteria: CPU > 80.0% of a core, or Memory growth >= 10,240 KiB per sample.) Tj ET
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 10.0 Tf 48.00 95.50 Td (•) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.0 Tf 59.00 95.50 Td (Persistence Rule: Requires exactly 3 consecutive samples exceeding threshold before confirming.) Tj ET
0.150 0.350 0.600 rg BT /F2 10.0 Tf 48.00 81.50 Td (•) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.0 Tf 59.00 81.50 Td (Active Suppression: Emits exactly ONE event upon confirmation; suppresses subsequent alarms while condition) Tj ET
0.150 0.150 0.150 rg BT /F1 9.0 Tf 59.00 69.50 Td (remains continuously active.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 45 30 Td (OS Process Guardian — Final Implementation & Validation Report) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 517.00 30 Td (Page 1 of 3) Tj ET
